WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.420 --> 00:00:05.170
The Eiffel Tower rises above the French capital.

00:00:05.170 --> 00:00:09.290
Known as the "Iron Lady", it stands 324-meters
tall.

00:00:09.290 --> 00:00:17.029
It's the tallest structure in Paris, offering
great views of the city and the River Seine.

00:00:17.029 --> 00:00:19.300
On the way to the top there are three platforms.

00:00:19.300 --> 00:00:23.390
Those who fancy the exercise can take the
stairs to the second platform.

00:00:23.390 --> 00:00:32.619
If you're heading to the top, be prepared
to climb the 1165 steps.

00:00:32.619 --> 00:00:36.629
Of course, you can always take the elevator.

00:00:36.629 --> 00:00:39.889
That's where you'll often find Karim Chaibi.

00:00:39.889 --> 00:00:42.920
He's been working at the Eiffel Tower for
15 years.

00:00:42.920 --> 00:00:55.559
He operates the elevator and talks to the
visitors in almost every language imaginable.

00:00:55.559 --> 00:00:59.139
Chaibi says there's no place he'd rather work.

00:00:59.139 --> 00:01:05.590
"You can get away from everyday worries with
a view like this.

00:01:05.590 --> 00:01:08.710
You see the city in a very interesting, architectural
way.

00:01:08.710 --> 00:01:15.680
And somehow you're a bit of a tourist and
feel as if you're on holiday."

00:01:15.680 --> 00:01:19.869
The stop for the first platform is nearly
60 meters up.

00:01:19.869 --> 00:01:23.700
Visitors are drawn out to the sun deck here
and the exhibition that takes them around

00:01:23.700 --> 00:01:25.100
the platform's perimeter.

00:01:25.100 --> 00:01:33.860
It tells the story of the Eiffel Tower.

00:01:33.860 --> 00:01:37.710
The Eiffel Tower wasn't always as popular
as it is today.

00:01:37.710 --> 00:01:43.680
When engineer Gustave Eiffel had it built
for the 1889 World's Fair, artists and intellectuals

00:01:43.680 --> 00:01:46.079
considered it common and lowly.

00:01:46.079 --> 00:01:51.479
Author Léon Bloy ironically described it
as a truly tragic streetlamp.

00:01:51.479 --> 00:01:56.780
That was a broadside at Eiffel's industrial
building methods, which contrasted sharply

00:01:56.780 --> 00:02:01.140
with the historical beauty of the city.

00:02:01.140 --> 00:02:05.170
The initial plan was to tear the tower down
after two decades.

00:02:05.170 --> 00:02:10.319
Architect Bertrand Lemoine explains why it's
still standing today.

00:02:10.319 --> 00:02:17.340
"Eiffel at some point got the idea that the
tower could be used as a place for a radio

00:02:17.340 --> 00:02:19.410
antenna.

00:02:19.410 --> 00:02:24.580
The French army was really interested and
began to do experiments and transmit.

00:02:24.580 --> 00:02:27.800
That made the tower strategically important.

00:02:27.800 --> 00:02:31.900
That's why they kept it."

00:02:31.900 --> 00:02:36.041
Impressive views can be had from all over
the tower – especially from the second and

00:02:36.041 --> 00:02:44.640
the third platforms.

00:02:44.640 --> 00:02:50.459
You can see many other Parisian sights from
here – including the Louvre – and the

00:02:50.459 --> 00:02:53.549
dome of Les Invalides.

00:02:53.549 --> 00:02:56.330
"The view changes all the time.

00:02:56.330 --> 00:02:57.659
It's never the same.

00:02:57.659 --> 00:03:02.000
What's really impressive is how the sky and
the tower influence each other.

00:03:02.000 --> 00:03:05.349
Here you're out in the elements, the wind,
rain and sun.

00:03:05.349 --> 00:03:12.010
You're never just IN Paris, but ABOVE it,
between the sky and the earth."

00:03:12.010 --> 00:03:17.180
That's made the Eiffel Tower one of the world's
best-loved landmarks, with up to 30 thousand

00:03:17.180 --> 00:03:19.269
visitors a day.

00:03:19.269 --> 00:03:25.120
You need to pay to get in – tickets cost
as much as 17 euros.

00:03:25.120 --> 00:03:29.240
"It's unbelievable – a once-in-a-lifetime
experience.

00:03:29.240 --> 00:03:31.879
I'm from Mexico and I'm really impressed.

00:03:31.879 --> 00:03:32.879
It's wonderful."

00:03:32.879 --> 00:03:39.549
"Knowing about the history and that it´s
more modern in addition to Paris's cityscape

00:03:39.549 --> 00:03:44.030
it's kind of interesting to think about how
that fits in with all of the older buildings."

00:03:44.030 --> 00:03:49.549
"Everybody come here and can feel happy and
realize a dream and feel good."

00:03:49.549 --> 00:04:00.450
A souvenir snapshot is de rigueur!

00:04:00.450 --> 00:04:09.140
Euromaxx viewers have sent us their favorite
Eiffel Tower photographs.

00:04:09.140 --> 00:04:19.140
"The tower is so famous that people come here
just to be photographed with it.

00:04:19.140 --> 00:04:21.070
So they can say, 'I was here.

00:04:21.070 --> 00:04:23.550
I was at the Eiffel Tower.'

00:04:23.550 --> 00:04:27.080
It's not just a monument; it's a symbol of
Paris."

00:04:27.080 --> 00:04:35.710
And after dark, every hour on the hour, the
tower is awash with flashing lights.

00:04:35.710 --> 00:04:43.160
Otherwise, the famous landmark simply glows
elegantly above the City of Light.

